(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the Volkswagen Emissions 'Defeat Device' Scandal \(2015\), detailing the algorithmic detection of laboratory test cycles, environmental impact, and the profound breach of the IEEE Code of Ethics.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Context and the Engineering Dilemma:) Tj
T*
(   - In the late 2000s, Volkswagen heavily marketed 'Clean Diesel' passenger cars in the United) Tj
T*
(   States and Europe, claiming to deliver high fuel economy, powerful engine torque, and ultra-low) Tj
T*
(   nitrogen oxide \(NOx\) emissions meeting stringent EPA Tier 2 Bin 5 standards.) Tj
T*
(   - Chemical Engineering Reality: Reducing harmful NOx emissions required injecting chemical urea) Tj
T*
(   \(AdBlue\) into Selective Catalytic Reduction \(SCR\) exhaust systems or using Lean NOx Traps.) Tj
T*
(   However, running full emission controls degraded vehicle acceleration, lowered fuel economy,) Tj
T*
(   and required frequent, expensive urea tank refills that customers disliked.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The 'Defeat Device' Software Algorithm:) Tj
T*
(   - Instead of redesigning the physical engine hardware, software engineers programmed an) Tj
T*
(   intentional defeat device into the Bosch EDC17 engine control unit \(ECU\) firmware.) Tj
T*
(   - Test Stand Detection Logic: The algorithm continuously monitored vehicle inputs: steering) Tj
T*
(   wheel position \(exactly 0 degrees stationary\), vehicle speed profile, atmospheric pressure, and) Tj
T*
(   engine runtime. If these variables matched the standardized EPA Federal Test Procedure \(FTP-75\)) Tj
T*
(   roller dynamometer test cycle, the ECU switched to 'Dyno Mode', activating full emission) Tj
T*
(   controls and passing tests with flying colors.) Tj
T*
(   - Real-World Operation: In normal road driving, as soon as the driver turned the steering) Tj
T*
(   wheel, the ECU switched to an illegal 'Road Mode', deactivating emission controls to deliver) Tj
T*
