(   [Problem Statement]: Deconstruct the Boeing 737 MAX Flight Control \(MCAS\) Failures \(2018-2019\), analyzing sensor redundancy flaws, pilot notification concealment, and systemic corporate governance breakdowns.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Aircraft Redesign Problem:) Tj
T*
(   - To compete rapidly with the Airbus A320neo, Boeing redesigned the 737 with larger, more) Tj
T*
(   fuel-efficient CFM LEAP-1B engines. Because the 737 has low ground clearance, the larger) Tj
T*
(   engines had to be mounted further forward and higher on the wings.) Tj
T*
(   - Aerodynamic Consequence: At high angles of attack \(AoA\), the forward engine nacelles) Tj
T*
(   generated upward aerodynamic lift, causing the aircraft's nose to pitch up non-linearly,) Tj
T*
(   increasing stall risk.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Maneuvering Characteristics Augmentation System \(MCAS\):) Tj
T*
(   - Software Workaround: Boeing implemented MCAS software inside the flight control computer.) Tj
T*
(   When high AoA was detected, MCAS automatically commanded the horizontal stabilizer trim) Tj
T*
(   jackscrew to push the aircraft's nose down, mimicking the handling characteristics of older 737) Tj
T*
(   models so airlines would not require expensive FAA simulator training for pilots.) Tj
T*
(   - Fatal Sensor Redundancy Flaw: The 737 MAX possessed two physical Angle-of-Attack \(AoA\) sensor) Tj
T*
(   vanes on the fuselage. Inexplicably, MCAS was designed to read data from only ONE sensor at a) Tj
T*
(   time, switching between sensors on alternating flights!) Tj
T*
(   - Catastrophic Failure Sequence: When a single AoA sensor failed \(due to physical bird strike) Tj
T*
(   or sensor calibration drift\), it falsely reported a high angle of attack. MCAS activated) Tj
T*
(   repeatedly, aggressively commanding maximum nose-down trim. Pilots struggled against the) Tj
T*
(   unexpected stabilizer runaway, unable to manually overpower the electric trim motor, leading to) Tj
T*
(   the crashes of Lion Air Flight 610 and Ethiopian Airlines Flight 302, killing 346 people.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Ethical, Safety, and Organizational Breakdowns:) Tj
T*
(   - Concealment from Flight Crews: Boeing actively removed all descriptions of MCAS from flight) Tj
T*
(   manuals and pilot training materials to protect the commercial 'same type rating' marketing) Tj
T*
(   claim.) Tj
T*
(   - Violation of Core Engineering Principles: In aviation safety engineering, a single point of) Tj
T*
(   failure must NEVER have catastrophic control authority over primary flight surfaces.) Tj
T*
(   Safety-critical systems require triple redundant cross-voting sensors.) Tj
T*
(   - Systemic Lesson: Commercial marketing pressures must never compromise basic aeronautical) Tj
T*
(   safety and transparency.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
ET

