(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the principles and architecture of Continuous Internal Assessment \(CIA\) and Relative Grading systems in university engineering education, formulating mathematical models for SGPA and CGPA.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Continuous Internal Assessment \(CIA\) Philosophy:) Tj
T*
(   - Traditional education systems relied exclusively on a single end-semester written) Tj
T*
(   examination, encouraging cramming and failing to assess sustained practical engineering) Tj
T*
(   competencies.) Tj
T*
(   - Continuous Internal Assessment \(CIA\) evaluates students holistically throughout the entire) Tj
T*
(   15-week academic semester through multi-faceted assessments: periodic surprise quizzes \(10%\),) Tj
T*
(   laboratory practical experiments and viva voce \(20%\), midterm examinations \(20%\), technical) Tj
T*
(   assignments/mini-projects \(10%\), and final comprehensive end-term examinations \(40%\). This) Tj
T*
(   enforces steady study habits and practical hands-on proficiency.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Relative Grading Mathematical Distribution:) Tj
T*
(   - In advanced engineering courses, exam difficulty varies significantly. Relative grading) Tj
T*
(   evaluates a student's performance relative to the statistical performance of their peer cohort,) Tj
T*
(   modeled via a Gaussian normal distribution characterized by class mean \(mu\) and standard) Tj
T*
(   deviation \(sigma\):) Tj
T*
(   - Grade 'O' \(Outstanding / 10 points\): Score >= mu + 1.5 * sigma) Tj
T*
(   - Grade 'A+' \(Excellent / 9 points\): mu + 1.0 * sigma <= Score < mu + 1.5 * sigma) Tj
T*
(   - Grade 'A' \(Very Good / 8 points\): mu + 0.5 * sigma <= Score < mu + 1.0 * sigma) Tj
T*
(   - Grade 'B+' \(Good / 7 points\): mu <= Score < mu + 0.5 * sigma) Tj
T*
(   - Grade 'B' \(Above Average / 6 points\): mu - 0.5 * sigma <= Score < mu) Tj
T*
(   - Grade 'C' \(Average / 5 points\): mu - 1.0 * sigma <= Score < mu - 0.5 * sigma) Tj
T*
(   - Grade 'D' \(Pass / 4 points\): mu - 1.5 * sigma <= Score < mu - 1.0 * sigma) Tj
T*
(   - Grade 'F' \(Fail / 0 points\): Score < mu - 1.5 * sigma or Score < absolute passing threshold.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. SGPA and CGPA Mathematical Formulations:) Tj
T*
(   - Semester Grade Point Average \(SGPA\): Sized across N courses registered in semester k, where) Tj
T*
(   C_i is course credit weight and G_i is numeric grade point awarded:) Tj
T*
(   SGPA = \( sum_{i=1}^{N} C_i * G_i \) / \( sum_{i=1}^{N} C_i \).) Tj
T*
(   - Cumulative Grade Point Average \(CGPA\): Sized across all M semesters completed to date:) Tj
T*
(   CGPA = \( sum_{j=1}^{M} sum_{i} C_{ij} * G_{ij} \) / \( sum_{j=1}^{M} sum_{i} C_{ij} \).) Tj
T*
(   - Cumulative performance reflects sustained academic discipline across theoretical lectures,) Tj
T*
(   design studios, and laboratory practicals.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
