(   [Problem Statement]: Deconstruct the Semiconductor Integrated Circuits Layout-Design Act \(SICLDA, 2000\) of India, explaining protected subject matter, registration criteria, duration of protection, and differences from patent law.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Legislative Background and Purpose of SICLDA:) Tj
T*
(   - Designing the physical 3D geometric layout topography of an integrated circuit requires) Tj
T*
(   millions of dollars in engineering effort and months of meticulous CAD layout. However, once) Tj
T*
(   fabricated, a competitor could chemically etch the plastic packaging, photograph the silicon) Tj
T*
(   surface under a microscope, and clone the mask layouts at a fraction of the cost.) Tj
T*
(   - In compliance with TRIPS Article 35, the Government of India enacted the Semiconductor) Tj
T*
(   Integrated Circuits Layout-Design Act \(SICLDA\) in 2000 to provide specialized intellectual) Tj
T*
(   property protection for original semiconductor layout topologies.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Protected Subject Matter and Registrability Criteria:) Tj
T*
(   - A 'Layout-Design' is defined as the three-dimensional disposition of the elements) Tj
T*
(   \(transistors, diodes, resistors\) and metallic interconnections on a semiconductor substrate.) Tj
T*
(   - Registrability Requirements:) Tj
T*
(   \(1\) Originality: The layout must be the result of the creator's own intellectual effort and not) Tj
T*
(   commonly known among layout designers at the time of creation.) Tj
T*
(   \(2\) Distinctiveness: Must be inherently capable of being distinguished from other existing) Tj
T*
(   layouts.) Tj
T*
(   \(3\) Commercial Exploitation Limitation: Must not have been commercially exploited anywhere in) Tj
T*
(   India or abroad prior to filing \(or within 2 years of initial commercial exploitation\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Key Legal Distinctions: SICLDA vs Patent Law:) Tj
T*
ET

