12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Deconstruct the engineering ethics and product safety frameworks governing Medical Electronic Devices, detailing IEC 60601-1 electrical safety standards, leakage current limits, and biocompatibility testing.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Safety-Critical Nature of Medical Electronic Devices:) Tj
T*
(   - Medical devices \(e.g. electrocardiographs, defibrillators, patient monitors, infusion pumps\)) Tj
T*
(   attach electrically to vulnerable human patients whose skin barrier impedance may be bypassed) Tj
T*
(   by conductive gels or internal catheters. A microscopic electrical current that would be) Tj
T*
(   imperceptible to a healthy hand can induce fatal ventricular fibrillation if conducted across) Tj
T*
(   the human heart.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. IEC 60601-1 International Electrical Safety Standard:) Tj
T*
(   - Classifies medical electrical equipment into safety categories:) Tj
T*
(   - Type B \(Body\): Equipment without conductive patient connection \(or grounded connection\).) Tj
T*
