(   [Problem Statement]: Deconstruct the architecture, specialized instruments, and experimental scope of an Analog Electronics and Circuit Simulation Laboratory in an ECE department.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Purpose and Pedagogy of the Analog Electronics Lab:) Tj
T*
(   - While modern technology is heavily computerized, physical signals begin and end as continuous) Tj
T*
(   analog voltages and currents. The Analog Electronics Laboratory develops the student's) Tj
T*
(   intuitive hardware mastery of non-linear semiconductor physics, transistor biasing, feedback) Tj
T*
(   stability, and linear amplification.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Laboratory Benchtop Instrumentation:) Tj
T*
(   - Triple-Output DC Power Supplies: Independent, isolated DC power rails \(+15V, -15V, +5V\) with) Tj
T*
(   adjustable current limiting to power discrete op-amp and BJT circuits safely.) Tj
T*
(   - Digital Storage Oscilloscopes \(DSOs\) with Dual-Channel Waveform Capture: Allowing) Tj
T*
(   simultaneous inspection of input excitation vs amplified/distorted output waveforms, evaluating) Tj
T*
(   phase shifts and clipping.) Tj
T*
(   - Low-Distortion Audio Function Generators: Emitting pure sinusoidal test signals from 1 Hz to) Tj
T*
(   20 MHz.) Tj
T*
(   - Precision Digital Multimeters \(6.5-Digit Bench DMMs\): Measuring microscopic DC bias voltages,) Tj
T*
(   quiescent collector currents, and resistor matching.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Experimental Curriculum & SPICE Simulation Synergy:) Tj
T*
(   - BJT and MOSFET Small-Signal Amplifiers: Designing Common-Emitter \(CE\) and Common-Source \(CS\)) Tj
T*
(   amplifiers; measuring voltage gain, input/output impedance, and 3-dB high/low frequency cutoff) Tj
T*
ET

