(   [Problem Statement]: Deconstruct the Challenger Space Shuttle Disaster \(1986\), analyzing O-ring cold-temperature resilience failure, management pressure, normalization of deviance, and the ethical responsibility of engineers to speak truth to power.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Mission and Environmental Context:) Tj
T*
(   - On January 28, 1986, the Space Shuttle Challenger broke apart 73 seconds after launch,) Tj
T*
(   killing all seven crew members. The morning of the launch, the launch pad at Kennedy Space) Tj
T*
(   Center experienced an unprecedented winter freeze, with ambient temperatures dropping to -1 deg) Tj
T*
(   C \(31 deg F\)?far below the qualified operational temperature envelope of the Solid Rocket) Tj
T*
(   Boosters \(SRBs\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Physical Mechanical Failure:) Tj
T*
(   - The giant Solid Rocket Boosters were manufactured in cylindrical segments by contractor) Tj
T*
ET

