45 780 Td
(   Morton Thiokol and assembled at the launch site. The joints between segments were sealed by two) Tj
T*
(   synthetic rubber \(Viton\) O-rings designed to expand and seal against hot, high-pressure) Tj
T*
(   combustion gases during launch.) Tj
T*
(   - Loss of Elastic Resilience: At cold temperatures near freezing, the Viton elastomer became) Tj
T*
(   stiff, losing its physical elasticity. When the rocket ignited, the cold primary O-ring failed) Tj
T*
(   to expand rapidly, allowing blow-by of searing 3,000 deg C combustion gases that burned through) Tj
T*
(   the joint, severing the SRB strut and penetrating the external liquid hydrogen/oxygen tank,) Tj
T*
(   causing a catastrophic structural explosion.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. The Tragic Ethical and Managerial Breakdown:) Tj
T*
(   - The Night-Before Teleconference: Morton Thiokol engineers \(led by Roger Boisjoly and Bob) Tj
T*
(   Ebeling\) recognized the extreme cold hazard. They presented experimental data showing past) Tj
T*
(   O-ring blow-by damage correlated directly with low temperatures, and unanimously recommended) Tj
T*
(   NOT LAUNCHING below 12 deg C \(53 deg F\).) Tj
T*
(   - Management Pressure & 'Take Off Your Engineering Hat': NASA managers, facing PR pressure) Tj
T*
(   regarding schedule delays, pushed back aggressively against the engineers' recommendation.) Tj
T*
(   Morton Thiokol senior executives caved to commercial client pressure, famously telling their) Tj
T*
(   engineering VP to 'take off your engineering hat and put on your management hat', overriding) Tj
T*
(   their own technical experts to sign the fatal launch approval.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Normalization of Deviance:) Tj
T*
(   - Sociologist Diane Vaughan termed NASA's organizational failure 'Normalization of) Tj
T*
(   Deviance'?because past shuttle launches had experienced partial O-ring erosion without) Tj
T*
(   catastrophic explosion, management falsely rationalized that future erosion was an acceptable) Tj
T*
(   operational risk rather than a severe warning of imminent failure.) Tj
T*
(   - Enduring Ethical Imperative: An engineer's primary ethical allegiance is to physical truth) Tj
T*
(   and human safety, never to bureaucratic schedule convenience.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
