(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the role and architecture of an Open-Source Software/Hardware Repository \(GitHub/GitLab\) in building an ECE undergraduate's technical portfolio, detailing README architecture, licensing, and reproducibility.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Digital Engineering Portfolio:) Tj
T*
(   - In the modern global technology sector, traditional paper resumes listing classroom course) Tj
T*
(   titles are insufficient. Elite semiconductor companies, embedded firmware firms, and robotics) Tj
T*
(   research laboratories evaluate candidates by inspecting their publicly verifiable code) Tj
T*
(   repositories and hardware projects on platforms like GitHub and GitLab.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Core Architecture of a World-Class Engineering Repository:) Tj
T*
(   - Comprehensive README.md: The visual front-door of the project. Must contain: \(1\) System) Tj
T*
(   Overview & Problem Statement; \(2\) Architectural Block Diagrams; \(3\) High-Resolution Photos of) Tj
T*
(   the Fabricated Physical PCB and Enclosure; \(4\) Annotated DSO/Logic Analyzer Waveform) Tj
T*
(   Screenshots proving live hardware functionality; \(5\) Quantitative Benchmark Tables comparing) Tj
T*
(   performance against literature.) Tj
T*
(   - Complete Design Source Files: Uploading full KiCad/Altium schematic and PCB layout files) Tj
T*
(   \(including manufacturing Gerbers and BOM\); synthesizable Verilog/SystemVerilog RTL and UVM) Tj
T*
(   testbenches; clean, modular C/C++ firmware with Makefiles or CMake build scripts.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Open-Source Licensing & Intellectual Property:) Tj
T*
(   - Permissive Licenses \(MIT, Apache 2.0, BSD\): Allow commercial and academic re-use with simple) Tj
T*
(   author attribution.) Tj
T*
(   - Hardware Open-Source Licenses \(CERN-OHL, TAPR OHL\): Tailored specifically for physical) Tj
T*
(   hardware designs, governing schematics, PCB layouts, and manufacturing rights.) Tj
T*
ET

